  "family": "Moraceae",
  "memo": "&lt;em&gt;Ficus microcarpa ‘Green Gem’&lt;/em&gt; is a cultivar of the Chinese banyan, valued for its dense, compact growth habit and small, glossy green leaves that are more tightly arranged than those of the species. In the wild, the parent species develops into a large tree, but it is widely cultivated as a houseplant and for bonsai due to its adaptability and tolerance of pruning. This cultivar is notably more compact and bushy, making it well-suited for container growing. It performs best in bright, indirect light with consistently moist, well-draining soil. Plants may be sensitive to abrupt changes in light or temperature, as well as stress from repotting. As with many indoor Ficus, it can also be susceptible to common houseplant pests, however it is resistant to thrips.&nbsp;",
